      "type": "textEditor",
      "data": {
        "value": "<p><strong>MINIMAL RESIDUAL DISEASE (MRD) ANALYSIS FOR AML</strong></p>\n<table class=\"Table cke_show_border\" style=\"width: 97.2833%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 39.7893%;\">\n<p><strong>Clinical history</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 60.2289%;\">\n<p>K/C/O Acute Myeloid Leukemia</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 39.7893%;\">\n<p><strong>Specimen</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 60.2289%;\">\n<p>Bone Marrow</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 39.7893%;\">\n<p><strong>Instrument software</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 60.2289%;\">\n<p>BD FACS LYRIC/BD FACS SUITE</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 39.7893%;\">\n<p><strong>Gating strategy</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 60.2289%;\">\n<p>10 colour FCM using CD 45 gating.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 39.7893%;\">\n<p><strong>Cell preparation method</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 60.2289%;\">\n<p>Stain - Lyse - Wash</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 39.7893%;\">\n<p><strong>Number of Events Acquired</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 60.2289%;\">\n<p>2500000</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><br><strong>Descriptive summary:</strong><br>Flow cytometric immunophenotypic analysis of the bone marrow was done on CD45/side scatter plots. A total of<br>25 lac events were acquired.</p>\n<p><br>CD34, CD117 used for gating and further hierarchial analysis shows a distinct cluster of cells with abnormal immunophenotype (CD34 moderate, Bright CD117, Bright HAL DR, Moderate CD13, Moderate CD33, Partial CD7). Immunophenotype similar to the diagnostic sample. These cells constitute ~0.8% of viable nucleated cells.</p>\n<p><br><strong>Minimal residual disease is POSITIVE.</strong></p>\n<p><br><strong>IMPRESSION: Flow cytometry analysis shows presence of residual disease.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Note:&nbsp;</strong><br>MRD results are to be correlated with the clinical details, diagnostic immunophenotype and cytogenetic profile of the patient.&nbsp;<br>MRD can be used as an independent prognostic factor for the patient, however its role for therapeutic decisions is to be based on the treatment protocol being used for the patient.</p>",
        "field": "textEditor"
      },
      "_id": "67b85ecf7d67ac81b08dc058"
    }
  ],
